# Web anti-pattern checker

Before finishing a React or TypeScript change under `apps/desktop/src` or `apps/landing/src`, inspect the touched files and list every violation below. Fix violations in the code you are already changing. List pre-existing violations in those files and leave them unless the user asked to clean them.

## Violations

- `any`, `as any`, or `@ts-ignore`.
- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or `eval`.
- An import from the other app (`apps/desktop` importing `apps/landing`, or the reverse).
- `invoke`, `fetch`, or a query call inside render or inside `.map` over the library.
- Server data copied into `useState` when a query already owns it.
- `useEffect` whose only job is to copy props or query data into state.
- A `listen` or timer effect with no cleanup.
- `key={index}` on a list the user can reorder, filter, or delete.
- A page file that also defines a hook, a store, and the Tauri call.
- An effect dependency that is a freshly created object or array and retriggers itself.
- Decoding full artwork blobs while rendering a thumbnail grid.
- Native `<details>` / `<summary>` for settings, launch, or details expandables. Use
  `CollapsiblePanel` (`components/ui/collapsible-panel.tsx`, shadcn/Radix Collapsible)
  with a Lucide icon. Native disclosure widgets look like a different product.
- Mixing native `<select>` with shadcn `Select` / `OptionSelect` on the same toolbar.
- Control heights other than the 48px couch-distance target on library, details, and
  settings chrome, or ad-hoc gaps that ignore the 8px spacing scale.

```tsx
// BAD — a new object dependency retriggers the effect forever
useEffect(() => { setRate(sample) }, [{ bytes }])

// GOOD — depend on the primitive values
useEffect(() => { setRate(bytes) }, [bytes])
```

```tsx
// BAD — native disclosure in Settings / game details
<details>
  <summary>Advanced launch options</summary>
  ...
</details>

// GOOD — shared shadcn Collapsible with an icon
<CollapsiblePanel title="Advanced launch options" icon={Terminal}>
  ...
</CollapsiblePanel>
```

## Report

End the web work with this list, or `None in the touched files.`

```
## Web anti-pattern violations
- `path:line` — violation — fix
```
